    "upstream.v165.message201": "{p0}, region <bbox>{p1}</bbox>",
    "upstream.v165.message202":
        "If the target includes <bbox>left top right bottom</bbox>, these are relative coordinates from 0–1000 for the full reference image, not pixels: pixel x = coordinate × reference-image width / 1000, pixel y = coordinate × reference-image height / 1000. The region is only for locating this layer; do not crop it into a new canvas, center it, or enlarge it. Preserve the original canvas and object position.",
    "upstream.v165.message203": "Experimental layer separation requires 2–8 layers, one per row; the first layer is the background image",
    "upstream.v165.message204": "Experimental layer-separation targets cannot repeat",
    "upstream.v165.message205": "Planned layer {p0} is missing independent generation parameters; layer-splitting task was not submitted",
    "upstream.v165.message206": "The independent prompt for planned layer {p0} is invalid; layer-splitting task was not submitted",
    "upstream.v165.message207": "The transparency parameter for planned layer {p0} conflicts with its layer role; layer-splitting task was not submitted",
    "upstream.v165.message208": "Planned layer {p0} contains unsupported generation parameters; layer-splitting task was not submitted",
    "upstream.v165.message209":
        "This is a complete, opaque background image; every pixel must have alpha=255. Remove the specified object and fill the occluded area while preserving the other environment, base colors, lighting, textures, and design structure. If the object to remove is a full photo, card, or panel, remove the entire block and its contents. Fill with the original background or environment; do not add the removed object back or add nonexistent objects. Do not use a transparent background or a semi-transparent base image.",
    "upstream.v165.message210":
        "This is an independent transparent object: retain only this layer's target, remove non-target content, and make blank areas true alpha=0 while preserving natural edges and ground shadow. If the target is a full photo, card, or panel, copy all original panel content (subject, internal scene, border, and rounded corners), keeping the inside opaque and making only the outside transparent. Do not cut out the subject inside the panel or enlarge it separately.",
    "upstream.v165.message211":
        "Output only one independent layer this time. {p0}\nLayer task: {p1}{p2}\n{p3}Preserve the reference image's full canvas size, original position, proportions, and details. Do not expand, crop, center, or rearrange. Output PNG; do not create a composite sheet, text annotations, or a checkerboard.",
